## 3. Evaluation Definitions

To ensure complete rigor before Phase 2 optimization, all metric definitions are frozen as follows:

1. **Hit Rate@K**:
   $$\text{Hit Rate}@K = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \mathbb{I}(\text{Gold}_i \cap \text{Retrieved}_{i, K} \neq \emptyset)$$

2. **Evidence Recall@K**:
   $$\text{Recall}@K = \frac{|\text{Gold} \cap \text{Retrieved}_K|}{|\text{Gold}|}$$

3. **Evidence Precision@K**:
   $$\text{Evidence Precision}@K = \frac{|\text{Retrieved}_K \cap (\text{PRIMARY} \cup \text{SUPPORTING})|}{K}$$

4. **Primary Precision@K**:
   $$\text{Primary Precision}@K = \frac{|\text{Retrieved}_K \cap \text{PRIMARY}|}{K}$$

5. **MRR (Mean Reciprocal Rank)**:
   $$\text{MRR} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \frac{1}{\text{rank of first useful chunk in } \text{Gold}_i}$$

6. **nDCG@10**:
   $$\text{nDCG}@10 = \frac{\text{DCG}@10}{\text{IDCG}@10}, \quad \text{DCG}@10 = \sum_{j=1}^{10} \frac{2^{\text{rel}_j} - 1}{\log_2(j + 1)}$$
   *Relevance Grading Scale*: `PRIMARY` = 3, `SUPPORTING` = 2, `RELEVANT_BUT_UNNECESSARY` = 1, `IRRELEVANT` = 0, `DUPLICATE` = 0.

7. **Evidence Completeness**:
   $$\text{Completeness} = \begin{cases} 1 & \text{if all PRIMARY gold chunks are present in Top-10} \\ 0 & \text{otherwise} \end{cases}$$

8. **Redundancy Ratio**:
   $$\text{Redundancy Ratio} = \frac{\text{Number of Top-K chunks sharing parent ID with an earlier chunk}}{K}$$

